## 8. Conclusion

The Datadog analysis identified significant performance and reliability problems affecting the production `customer-api` service.

The `/api/v1/checkout` endpoint reached a p95 latency of **4650 ms** and an error rate of **12%**.

The `/api/v1/cards/charge` endpoint reached a p95 latency of **5200 ms** and an error rate of **14%**.

Both endpoints exceeded the configured critical thresholds of **4000 ms p95 latency** and **10% error rate**, so both should be considered **CRITICAL**.

The `/api/v1/customers` endpoint remained healthy with a p95 latency of **195 ms** and an error rate of only **0.1%**.

Datadog facets such as `@http.status_code`, `@customer.tier`, `@error.type`, and `@duration_ms` provide additional dimensions for troubleshooting. Combining these facets with p95 latency and error-rate monitoring provides stronger visibility into production API failures.
